-- title:
--   Semilinear chart automorphism at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, $\ell\nmid M'$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of order $q\ell$, with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th and $\xi$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ for the subgroup $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, uniformiser $\varpi$, and compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$; let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have Laurent expansion the $q$-expansion `jq` of the $j$-function. Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $X=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel` $A\,K\,j$ at which the germ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra $\mathcal A_{\mathrm{fin}}=$ `chartAlgFin` map to $z$, and assume $y$ is supersingular: every ring map $\varphi$ from $\mathcal A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ to an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ sends `jChartFin` into `ssJSet` $q$, i.e. to a $j$-invariant all of whose elliptic curves have trivial $q$-torsion. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma:A\to W$ a ring map with maximal ideal of $W$ generated by $\sigma\varpi$, let $u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ be units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v-fu)$ which reads constants, i.e. sends the image of the germ of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$. The assertion: for all ring automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and $\sigma_A$ of $A$ compatible under $A\to L$ with $\sigma_A a\equiv a$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting on Laurent series by `coeffMap` $\sigma_L$ such that $\tau$ and $\tau^{-1}$ preserve $\mathcal A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\tau a-a\in y$ for all $a\in\mathcal A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ and a ring automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W$ with $\theta\circ e\circ(\text{completion of the germ at }z)=e\circ(\text{completion of the germ at }z)\circ\tau$ on $\mathcal A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, with $\sigma_W\circ\sigma=\sigma\circ\sigma_A$ on $A$, with $\sigma_W w\equiv w$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, and with $\theta$ sending the class of $C(w)$ to the class of $C(\sigma_W w)$ for all $w\in W$.
--
--   This is the transport step in the Drinfeld-chart analysis of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: an automorphism of the finite chart algebra that is coefficientwise Galois on Laurent expansions and congruent to the identity at the chosen prime is carried, through the chart isomorphism $e$, to a $\sigma_W$-semilinear automorphism of $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v-fu)$ whose action on constants is pinned down. It supplies the first four clauses of the inertia statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_diagOneElem_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.inertia_drinfeldChart_semilinear_linearPart_diagOneElem_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel), where the linear part of $\theta$ on $(X_0,X_1)$ is then computed.
